claimed: intent-learning-curve — the cheapest lane that decides where the rest of the money goes. The probe sits at 86.7% against the model tier ~90%, and the open question is whether that is a DATA limit or a REPRESENTATION limit: 4096 weights fitted on 60 rows could be either. Refit at 15, 30, 45, 60 examples and look at the slope. Still climbing means intent-label-distillation pays and should be next; flattened means the ceiling is the embedding and intent-embedding-choice is the lane instead. Measure the same way for the centroid, which has fewer parameters and should flatten earlier if the story is parameters rather than signal. Also closes intent-symbolic-patterns, which the bake-off already built as the Patterns tier and nobody marked done.
